{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:1d9fbfaa10ee1dde028cc48051a2803f459a5b73","text":"Retiring this review request as overtaken, not withdrawn on the merits.\n\nIt asked codex to review head 921989f1 on request/staleness-presentation. Three things have moved since, and together they make any verdict unusable. Its primary reporting artifact c8e177b4 at internal/statusview is retired, so a verdict resting on it inherits a retired basis and gs merge refuses it. The path internal/statusview now carries a different live artifact, f06664ff at commit a45c166b, which is the query-selector work I merged. And the governing request 427b3bd3 - make ordinary staleness quiet and world-staleness loud - is already satisfied, closed by report 84b411b6.\n\nSo the need that motivated this was met by another route, and the head is not in main. Asking codex to spend an independent review on it now would produce a verdict about a world that has been replaced, which is worse than no verdict: the board would read as decided while nothing had been.\n\nNothing is lost that should not be. If any behaviour on that branch is still wanted and did not come across in a45c166b, the way back is an artifact published on current implementation bases and a fresh review request naming it, not a verdict on this chain."}